I don't really know how else we'd do something like 

```jsonc
        {
            "iterateOn": "profiles",
            "icon": "${profile.icon}",
            "name": "New tab with ${profile.name}",
            "command": { "action": "newTab", "profile": "${profile.name}" }
        },
```

the trick here is that any of the args in the command might have also had "${profile.name}" in them. We don't know which ones did or didn't really. What about:


```jsonc
        {
            "iterateOn": "profiles",
            "name": "Rename tab to ${profile.name}",
            "command": { "action": "renameTab", "title": "${profile.name}" }
        },
```

that's a silly example, but it's _valid_

Or:
```jsonc
        {
            "iterateOn": "profiles",
            "name": "Make three ${profile.name} splits",
            "command": { "action": "wt", "commandline": "sp -p ${profile.name} ; sp -p ${profile.name} ; sp -p ${profile.name}" }
        },
```

less silly, and _harder_ to detect

